  "notes": "West cashes the ♣K, ♠K, ♠A, and ♣A before exiting with the ♣J for South to ruff. South should draw trump ending in dummy and lead a diamond. South can afford 1 diamond loser, but not 2. In order to make the contract, South must guess whether to play the ♦K or the ♦J.\n\nIf East has the ♦Q and West has the ♦A, it is necessary to play the ♦J. West will win the ♦A and South will make the contract. West has already shown up with 15 high card points, however. The ♦A would make 19 points, too much for a 1NT opening bid.\n\nEast must have the ♦A and, if West has the ♦Q, it will be fatal to play the ♦J. South must instead play the ♦K. When that holds the trick, South makes his contract.",
